    "result_text": "Each invoice now shows its effective tax rate as a percentage, and `bin/e2e` passes. In the test case (20% tax, a 200 taxable line and a 100 tax-free line) it shows **13.33%**.\n\n**How it's worked out:** the sales tax and the levy added together, divided by the invoice's \"Total before tax\", rounded to two decimal places. Two choices you may want to check:\n- **The levy is included.** You asked for the overall rate, and the levy is a second tax, so I counted it. Your test has no levy, so it doesn't decide this either way.\n- **I divided by the total before tax, not the raw subtotal.** The test's comment says \"of the subtotal\", and in its case the two are the same (300). They only differ when there's a discount or the prices already include tax. In those cases the total before tax still gives the true rate, while the subtotal would understate it.\n\nIf there's nothing before tax (for example, an invoice with no lines), it shows 0.00%.\n\n**No database migration was needed.** The rate is calculated from figures each invoice already stores, so a sent invoice keeps the rate it was issued with.\n\n**What changed:**\n- **Server:** a new `getEffectiveTaxPct()` in `Invoice.java`, returned as `effectiveTaxPct` in `InvoiceDetailResponse`.\n- **Front end:** the field is added to `InvoiceDetail` in `invoice.service.ts`. In `invoice-detail.ts` there's a new \"Effective tax rate\" row just above \"Total before tax\", with `data-testid=\"invoice-effective-tax-rate\"`. No existing test IDs were changed.",
